<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Bytom</h1><p class="st-meta">1281 CE – 1498 CE (approx.) · capital Bytom</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Upper Silesian Piast duchy whose first duke became the first Silesian prince to pay homage to the King of Bohemia, in 1289.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-of-opole">Władysław of Opole</a> died in 1281, his lands were divided among his sons. Casimir received <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bytom">Bytom</a>, an old market town in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-silesia">Upper Silesia</a>, together with lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gliwice">Gliwice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kozle">Koźle</a>. In 1289 he paid homage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wenceslaus-ii-of-bohemia">Wenceslaus II of Bohemia</a>, the first Silesian duke to accept Bohemian overlordship.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The duchy was small, with farmland, forests and early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and lead mining around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bytom">Bytom</a>. Casimir's son Władysław ruled it in the early 14th century, and later dukes divided it into smaller shares. The population was largely Polish-speaking, with German settlers in the towns.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bytom">Bytom</a> line died out in 1355, the duchy was divided between the dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olesnica">Oleśnica</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cieszyn">Cieszyn</a> and later fragmented further, with parts passing among Silesian princes until the end of the 15th century. It eventually came under the Bohemian crown, and Bytom is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-bytom.jpg" alt="Duchy of Bytom" width="320" height="288"><figcaption>Image: Tymoteusz Trzewiczek · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C5%9Al%C4%85sk_1284-1287.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1281 CE – 1498 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bytom</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Casimir of Bytom, Władysław of Bytom</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Polish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Duchy of Beuthen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1390&amp;focus=duchy-of-bytom" aria-label="Duchy of Bytom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5112 428 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Bytom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5432 684L5408 675M5432 684L5330 692M5432 684L5415 685"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5408 675h0M5330 692h0M5415 685h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5432 684h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5432 684h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bytom. <a href="/atlas?year=1390&amp;focus=duchy-of-bytom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
